{
    "_doc": "Demand of permission_sex_unprotected_penis (its demandEventID, Docs/Interactions/Plan_PermissionApplicability.md): the penis owner's side of OnAPRefuse_Unprotected - started by ActionPackage.TryStopForDemand when the granter (penis owner) ACCEPTED putting their bare penis into the requester's vagina but has not allowed going bare. self = the requester (permission holder, the vagina owner), evTarget = the granter. Code (ActionPackage.SendDemandEvent) builds StoredOptions[demandOptions]: the condom answers (the wearer is the granter: put it on $evTarget$ / $evTarget$ puts it on themselves - both immediate, the act resumes) and, because the permission sets demandSafeDayClaim, the safe-day claim: say today is safe (a lie when self is on a danger day). The claim is the granter's request decision for this permission (no roll; the option tooltip shows it): accepted = a Temporary grant (ends with the scene) and the act resumes (br_claim / br_claim_lie), refused = the granter's refusal line and the question again without the claim (br_claim_refused -> br_choice_noclaim, StoredOptions[demandOptionsNoClaim]). The event's own options: ignore the demand (apCallback: records the scene push and resumes the act) or give up (failCallback). An NPC requester decides in code (condom now if possible, else the claim if the granter would accept, else ignore) and starts at that answer's line. Kojo (speaker = evTarget, the penis owner): permission_sex_unprotected_penis_Demand / _Ignored / _SafeDay_Accepted / _SafeDay_Refused. br_condom_self / br_condom_partner are the requester-wears answers, kept for a requester whose own penis is the act's. File name contains sex: safe mode skips it.",
